  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list is ready under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies are booked. Three cancelled appointments (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) were left off and got no orders.\n\n**Results that came in while I worked:** four arrived at 08:00, one for each patient. They changed the plans for pt-0047, pt-0015 and pt-0049. I changed those orders, sent each of those patients a corrected message, and closed all four inbox items.\n\n**1. pt-0047 Britt Mohr – CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast, 08:00 (sr-t0001)**\n- He has type 2 diabetes managed by diet only. His last creatinine (9/24) was more than 30 days old, so I ordered a creatinine drawn before the scan (sr-t0009).\n- New outside labs show his creatinine rose from 1.04 on 10/21 to 1.52 on 10/22, which counts as acute kidney injury.\n- I kept the pre-scan creatinine and added 0.9% saline 500 mL IV at 07:00 (mr-t0016). No allergy, no premedication, no metformin.\n- Messages: comm-t0011, then the corrected one comm-t0021 (arrive about 06:45).\n\n**2. pt-0015 Daniel Ferreira – CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast, 09:00 (sr-t0002)**\n- His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis\" to iohexol, but that was his own account. The 2019 radiology report graded the reaction moderate, so the policy's premedication applies.\n- Premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 20:00 on 10/25 and at 02:00 and 08:00 on 10/26 (mr-t0005), plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0006). He needs a driver.\n- His 10/14 creatinine was corrected from 0.98 (another patient's sample) to 2.8, an eGFR of 24. I added saline 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0017).\n- Messages in Spanish and English: comm-t0012, then corrected comm-t0022.\n- I created an urgent task for you (task-t0028): a creatinine of 2.8 with no known kidney disease needs workup.\n\n**3. pt-0049 Anisha Schuster – CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast, 13:00 (sr-t0003)**\n- She had acute kidney injury at the ED on 10/04 and her creatinine hasn't been rechecked since, so it is treated as still present.\n- Orders: pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0010) and saline 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0007).\n- Metformin (mr-00392) is on hold for 10/26 and at least 48 hours after the scan. Your task task-t0015 (due 10/28) is to recheck kidney function before restarting it.\n- An outside report from 2022 shows a moderate reaction to iopamidol. I added prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0018) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0019). She needs a driver.\n- Messages: comm-t0013, then updated comm-t0023.\n- The iopamidol allergy is not on her allergy list yet, because the catalog had no code for it. Please add it.\n\n**4. pt-0046 Lauren Beahan – CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast (stone protocol), 14:00 (sr-t0004)**\n- Ordered as booked; a scan without contrast needs no prep. Message: comm-t0014.\n- An outside report shows a mild reaction to iohexol in 2024. I added it to her allergy list (alg-t0020); it doesn't affect Monday's scan.\n\nEach of the four has a signed note citing RBC-RAD-07 (doc-t0024 to t0027).\n\n**Not touched:** inbox items that were already open before I started and are unrelated to this list. They include critical potassium results for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4), which need your attention.",
